=== reduced-footnotes
The sample mean ⟨$\bar{X}_n$⟩ of ⟨$n$⟩ independent draws converges in distribution.1 The rate depends on the variance ⟨$\sigma^2$⟩.2
For i.i.d. ⟨$X_i$⟩ with mean ⟨$\mu$⟩ and variance ⟨$\sigma^2 < \infty$⟩,
⟦$$\sqrt{n},(\bar{X}_n - \mu) \xrightarrow{d} \mathcal{N}(0, \sigma^2).$$⟧
The Berry-Esseen bound gives ⟨$\sup_x |F_n(x) - \Phi(x)| \le \frac{C \rho}{\sigma^3 \sqrt{n}}$⟩ with ⟨$C < 0.48$⟩, where ⟨$\rho = E|X - \mu|^3$⟩.
